Homepage: https://github.com/ra-yavuz/portunus-ovpn
Description: KDE Plasma 6 panel widget for switching OpenVPN connections
 portunus-ovpn is a native KDE Plasma 6 panel widget that imports, edits,
 removes, exports and toggles OpenVPN connections through NetworkManager.
 One VPN can be active at a time by default; multiple-active mode is
 available for split-tunnel combinations.
 .
 The widget drives the standard nmcli + NetworkManager + KWallet stack
 that ships with KDE. There is no second VPN daemon, no third-party PPA,
 and no parallel secret store.
 .
 DISCLAIMER: provided AS IS, no warranty. Toggles VPN connections, runs
 nmcli on your behalf, imports profile files (including private keys),
 and asks NetworkManager + KWallet to store key passphrases for you. The
 author is not liable for any damage to hardware, data, network, traffic
 exposure, or security. You are responsible for the contents of the
 .ovpn profiles you import. See /usr/share/doc/portunus-ovpn/README.md
 for the full disclaimer.
